Z||000012||AusFiero||06-02-2001||04:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>Long enough to know it costs a lot of money to keep them fixed and on the road!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>heheh Come to Australia. I have paid more for some parts than you guys have paid for Fieros  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>But I suppose I get the looks to go with such a rare car here. <P>I have had mine 2 1/2 years and is the longest I have owned any car out of the 46 I have had so the Fiero must have something going for it.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Alex4mula||06-02-2001||09:38 AM||||13 years now. Ordered my Formula to factory on December 1987 and was delivered beginning of April 1988. My daily driver since then. 168K miles.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ken Wittlief||06-02-2001||10:27 AM||||I have to admit when the Fiero first came out I wasnt real impressed with it. it looked sorta cool, but I thought there was something odd about the wheel wells, like the tires were too small for the openings in the body or something - way too small.<P>  I was into VW bugs back then, and had a bit of an anti-american car thing going on too. Mostly cause the only american car I had owned was a 69 cougar - which had serious unibody structural weakness design flaws. With all the junk that was coming out of detroit in the 80's it was hard to take any american car seriously.<P>   To save some face here, since I have owned a Fiero for about a month now, there are a lot of things wrong with mine, just about every major component or system on the car has something wrong with it, and needs to be fixed - so I guess my original assesment wasnt really wrong.<P>  detroit really turned things around in the '90s - too late for the Fiero though.||||reg||1
Z||000015||88formula||06-02-2001||10:32 AM||||Two years this September. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
