Z||000021||Formula88||06-02-2001||01:39 PM||||Well, I got my 1st Fiero, an 88 Formula - 5 speed, on January 29, 2001.  But, my good friend, LZeitgeist, has had Fieros for about 10 years or so and he's the one who got me hooked.  I've been "into" Fieros since they were new.  I bought my first (and only, to date) brand new car in the Fall of '87.  It was an '87 Buick Grand National.  I came SOOO close to getting a brand new loaded 88 Fiero GT!  But I decided to go with the GN because of the power, and with the clearance discounts since it was an 87 and the 88's were already coming out, it was too good a deal to pass up.  Now, if I had it to do over - especially if I'd known the Fiero was gonna be cancelled - oh yeah, gimme that GT baby! (I didn't know about Formulas at the time)||||reg||6
Z||000022||qwikgta||06-02-2001||01:42 PM||||I first sat in a fiero in July of 83 at the Pontiac-Oakland club show in Niagara Falls.  I first owned one in 89, picked up a 87 GT.  I loved that car.  I have two coupes now, one (87) I got at a repo sale for $200 the other my 88 TTop I got for $1200 off a local lot.  I'd get more but I have no space for them.<P>Rob ||||reg||1
Z||000023||LZeitgeist||06-03-2001||10:03 AM||||Back in '85, summer up in Minnesota, my aunt owned a black '84 Coupe and let me take it out for a spin while we were staying with them for a few days on their farm... didn't know anything about it other than it was kinda exotic and pretty sweet for an "aunt's car"...<P>In '87 or so, I test-drove a fully-loaded '87 GT, burgundy with silver, grey interior, full leather, etc. - and, get this - stereo controls in the steering wheel. (I WANT THAT!!!!!!) I fell in love, but it was way out of my budget back then. Might as well have been a Ferrari for all the chance there was of me getting it. But I loved it.<P>In something like May of 1990, I was out looking at used cars with a friend of mine, and I saw this red '88 Coupe... being Sunday, the dealership was closed, but I was curious enough to go back the next day for a test drive, for the sole reason of wanting to see the inside to see what would have to be changed to make it into a convertable. (It was strictly a theoretical situation for me.. I was just curious. All I had was a 2-year old Kawasaki EX-500 motorcycle and a LeCar I cut the top off of... nothing they'd take as a trade.)<P>So, I drove it around a bit, and by the time I got back to the dealership, I was thinking, "Daaaaamn... O.K., I want it.,, *sigh*"... but when I went to the salesman with my prepared line of "Well, all I have for trade-in is this motorcycle, and I know you won't want that, so I guess I'll have to let it go...", the salesman said "We can do that..."<P>!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<P>So, we worked out the trade, my sister helped me get financing, and away we went. <P>9 years and over 200,000 miles later, I had a Kawasaki Concours sport-touring bike and an '82 Fierbird I had hoped of converting into a showcar, so I'd just dumped 2 grand into a new engine for it, and my Fiero, who had been needing a *lot* of attention lately... I needed to get rid of a car, and it was a choice of either keeping the near dead Fiero, or keeping the ragged-out '82 Firebird that I'd just dumped a new engine into. It was tough, but it seemed the wiser choice was keeping the car with the new engine. So, I decided to sell the Fiero for $1000, which was the payoff on the loan for the engine. <P>I really didn't want to sell it, 'cause I'd loved the crap outta that car - it fit me sooo perfectly - but ya gotta do what makes sense. My folks knew I loved that car, so Dad, being newly retired, wanted to buy it from me as something to tinker on. So, they paid off the loan on the engine, and I gave them the Fiero. <P>For the next year or so, I was deeeeeeeep into withdrawal. Man, I never knew my emotional state could be altered by the lack of a friggin' car. Meanwhile, Dad got the Coupe running good, and *every* time I called over there, Mom would have to take the cordless phone outside to where Dad was *still* tinkering on the car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I got my kicks on the Concours, and I'd cruise in my ugly Firebird with the T-tops out to try and make myself feel better, but it just wasn't the same.<P>So, about a year and a half ago, I was on the bike headed out to get oil and a filter for it, and I spotted this *gorgeous*, nearly showroom-new-looking Formula in a used car lot. I taked to the owner the next day, and traded the motorcycle for it on the spot. I can always get another Concours (they've made them for the last 15 years...), but they only made the Formula for ONE.  <P>And now Dad is hooked, too... we swapped noses and tails on the Coupe with thse from a junked GT, painted it and created *our* version of a car Dad loved up in Virginia last year... so now we have an '88 Indy II. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> (And we've even got a spare V6 to drop in it when the old 4-cyl. gives up the ghost... but it's got 254,000 miles on it and still going, so it may be a while...)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000024||CoolBlue87GT||06-03-2001||11:35 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MrFeeArrow:<BR><B>Anyone have family Fiero's out there they still own?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>11/15/83 My first was a Red 84 4 cyl Sunroof,tilt,Radio: UU6 w/5 band EQ ($490)<BR>Wheels: WS6 Cast alum ($459), V58 Luggage carrier, cruise, Air<BR>         VIN: 1G2AM37R9EP215054<P>03/13/85 Traded in 84, Bought Red 85 SE V6 ($595), I had the dealer install radio from the 84 in the car. (It sounded much better).<BR>Sunroof,Pwr locks/windows,Tilt,Leather wheel,Alum whls($459), cruise, Air<BR>         VIN: 1G2PF3793FP224466<P>Both red cars looks the same from the outside, of course the V6 sounded better !<P>11/86  Traded the 85 on 87 GT V6  Took delivery, w/ 106 miles, Now, today has 1760 miles !<BR>Sunroof,pwr lock/windows/mirrors, Air,cruise,AM/FM/Cass w/Eq & Sub woofer<BR>Wheel locks, Whale tail<P>Has been known as FieroDave2001, now is CoolBlue87GT<P>I've had a Fiero ever since they came out.<P>Hope you enjoy the info. What ya think ?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CoolBlue87GT.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 06-03-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000025||Fiero Sam||06-03-2001||11:46 AM||||I got my 87 Coupe at the end of 89.I can still show you where she was sitting the first time I saw her.She has not cost me very much to keep her going.Only broke down twice and once was the fan belt(so that doesn't even count).||||reg||1
Z||000026||JetroGT||06-03-2001||02:27 PM||||I'm on my 4th and 5th fiero since 94. My first fiero was a gold 2M4. I was bussed to Six Flags Great America for a full year before I saved enough for it. My parents would not help out at all. Now I can see where they were comming from. Then..<P>86 GT Red Auto.<P>86 GT Black Auto. Bought with major damage for parts<P>86 SE Black Auto. Still driving it.<P>87 GT Blue 5spd. Loving it! And still being restored.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/JetroGTsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
